---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components

This repository builds on the GGPP release:

  Prompt-Perturbation-in-Retrieval-Augmented-Generation
  https://github.com/Hadise-zb/Prompt-Perturbation-in-Retrieval-Augmented-Generation

That release ships no licence file. Its code is therefore kept out of this repository
wherever that is practical. The two files this package imports from are generated
locally instead:

  DGD/DGD.py             byte-identical upstream copy, used as the "original" arm
  DGD/help_functions.py  upstream file plus a switchable query-wrapper parameter

Run `python tools/fetch_upstream.py` to obtain them from the upstream repository.
Both paths are git-ignored and are never committed.

One file is kept in the repository although it is derived from upstream:

  SFR_mistral_IMDB_rank.ipynb   the upstream notebook with cell 17 (the attack loop)
                                replaced; the other 17 cells are byte-identical to
                                the upstream release

It is retained so that the notebook route stays visible and runnable without a
generation step. Its copyright remains with the upstream authors and the MIT licence
above does not extend to it. The exact difference is recorded in
tools/SFR_mistral_IMDB_notebook.diff, and tools/build_rank_notebook.py can regenerate
it from the upstream file.

If you use any of the above, cite the original paper (see CITATION.cff).

Everything else in this repository - the rank-aware optimizer, the evaluation harness,
the tests and the tooling - is this project's own work and falls under the MIT licence
above.
